<!--Render Target — SentinelToggle
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.SentinelToggle-->
<render:SentinelToggle xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:render="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render">

  <baseType>
    core:Block
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Checkbox plus one value for a two-arm union
  </is>
  <documentation>
    One customizer rule. It matches a property union of exactly two named
    alternatives: the sentinel type, and the value type. Type arguments on
    the value arm are ignored, so Decimal(GridUnitZ) matches Decimal.

    checkboxSelects is sentinel or value. sentinel means the checkbox shows
    the constant (checked is "auto"). value means the checkbox shows that
    the other arm is in use (checked is the text or the path).

    checkboxSuffix is appended to the property name for the checkbox.
    The value field keeps the property name. The hidden result is
    hlp_ plus the property name plus Resolved.

    inactiveDefault is the SCAD literal of the value field while the
    property holds the sentinel. The sentinel literal itself is read from
    the constant type and serialized like any other property value.
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <sentinel type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        FQN of the constant alternative, such as com.machineblocks.bml.type.Auto.
      </documentation>
    </sentinel>
    <valueType type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        FQN of the other alternative, without type arguments.
        The first catalog accepts Decimal, Text, and FilePath.
      </documentation>
    </valueType>
    <checkboxSelects type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        sentinel or value. Which arm is used when the checkbox is checked.
      </documentation>
    </checkboxSelects>
    <checkboxSuffix type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        Appended to the property name to form the checkbox variable.
      </documentation>
    </checkboxSuffix>
    <inactiveDefault type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        SCAD literal shown in the value field when the property holds the sentinel.
      </documentation>
    </inactiveDefault>
  </properties>
</render:SentinelToggle>
